        "date":  "2025-05-19",
        "theme":  "Agents",
        "summary":  "Microsoft announced its vision for an open agentic web where AI agents make decisions and perform tasks on behalf of users and organizations. The company unveiled new AI development tools across GitHub, Azure AI Foundry, and Windows, along with enterprise-grade agent capabilities and support for open protocols like Model Context Protocol. Microsoft also introduced Microsoft Discovery, a platform designed to accelerate scientific research through agentic AI.",
        "execSummary":  "Microsoft\u0027s Build 2025 keynote declared the enterprise shift from AI copilots to autonomous AI agents capable of orchestrating multi-step work across platforms. For enterprise leaders, the critical move is Microsoft\u0027s endorsement of open interoperability standards — particularly the Model Context Protocol — which signals a platform strategy rather than a proprietary lock-in play. Organizations investing in AI agent infrastructure now should verify their tooling aligns with these emerging open standards. The caveat: agentic autonomy at scale introduces new governance and oversight requirements that most enterprises are not yet equipped to handle.",
