        "source":  "Google AI Blog",
        "url":  "https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/technology/developers-tools/antigravity-teamwork-multi-agent/",
        "date":  "2026-08-31",
        "theme":  "Orchestration",
        "summary":  "Google\u0027s Antigravity Teamwork framework enables autonomous AI agent teams to collaborate on complex challenges by orchestrating multiple specialized agents in parallel. When paired with Gemini 3.7 Flash, the system solved seven open mathematics problems, created a functional RISC-V CPU simulator, and contributed performance improvements to major open-source libraries. The results demonstrate that multi-agent orchestration can tackle problems beyond the reach of any single-model approach.",
        "execSummary":  "Google\u0027s Antigravity Teamwork results are a concrete proof point that multi-agent orchestration is crossing from research novelty into practical engineering capability. For enterprise AI leaders, the implication is that complex, multi-step business workflows — contract analysis, supply chain optimization, tiered support resolution — are now viable targets for agent orchestration rather than single-model automation. The open-source contributions are a credibility signal, but enterprise adoption requires production-grade reliability and audit trails that benchmark papers do not address. This is a technology to pilot in bounded, high-complexity workflows before committing to broad deployment.",
        "vendorLean":  "Google",
        "imageUrl":  null,
        "isNew":  false
