        "execSummary":  "The Model Hardware Standard represents Anthropic moving from pure language-model provision toward defining the interoperability layer for physical-world AI agent deployment. For enterprise leaders, the strategic implication is broader than lab automation — a vendor-neutral standard for agent-to-hardware control sets the pattern for how AI agents will eventually orchestrate enterprise operational technology, from logistics to manufacturing to facilities management. Adoption at Genentech and Carnegie Mellon gives the standard credibility in high-stakes environments. Watch whether this evolves into an industry-wide standard or becomes a proprietary moat disguised as openness.",
