        "title":  "How Frontier Teams Are Reinventing AI-Native Development",
        "source":  "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "url":  "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/how-frontier-teams-are-reinventing-ai-native-development/",
        "date":  "2026-06-10",
        "theme":  "Strategy",
        "summary":  "Leading engineering teams are redesigning software development workflows around AI agents, reporting productivity gains of 4.5x to 10x. The article identifies five key practices: investing in agent context, restructuring workflows before tool adoption, maintaining clear task backlogs, defining explicit requirements, and shifting testing earlier in the development cycle.",
        "execSummary":  "The productivity gains documented here — a 30-person 18-month project completed in 76 days via Amazon Bedrock — represent a step-change in enterprise software delivery economics, not an incremental improvement. The critical finding is that workflow restructuring must precede AI tool deployment; teams that simply add AI to existing processes see minimal gains. For CIOs and transformation leaders, this means AI-native development requires organizational redesign, not just tooling purchases. The caveat: these gains are concentrated in structured engineering tasks; creative and judgment-intensive work shows far less uplift.",
