        "theme":  "Support",
        "summary":  "This post demonstrates building a multimodal WhatsApp ordering assistant using Amazon Bedrock AgentCore and Amazon Nova 2 models that handles text messages, voice notes, and voice calls on a single business number. Shared memory across all channels delivers a unified customer experience regardless of interaction modality.",
        "execSummary":  "This reference architecture is a concrete signal of where enterprise customer engagement is heading: omnichannel AI agents that handle voice, text, and image inputs through a single intelligent interface on consumer messaging platforms. For customer support and digital commerce leaders, WhatsApp\u0027s global reach combined with multimodal AI dramatically lowers the cost of high-quality service at scale without forcing customers onto proprietary apps. The key operational implication is that shared cross-channel memory is now achievable in production, enabling agents to maintain context even when customers switch between voice and text mid-interaction. Teams evaluating conversational AI vendors should benchmark multimodal capability and channel unification as first-class requirements.",
