        "execSummary":  "The central tension in enterprise AI right now is not build-vs-buy — it is speed-vs-control, and most organizations are losing on both sides by trying to split the difference rather than sequencing deliberately. CIOs who are winning have established independent AI governance functions before scaling, not after, which means the compliance investment precedes the innovation spend. For customer-support leaders, the practical implication is that your AI deployment roadmap needs a governance gate: every new agent or automation capability should pass a risk assessment checkpoint before it touches a customer. The caveat to watch is that governance structures built too rigidly today will slow adaptation as models and regulations evolve rapidly through 2027.",
