        "execSummary":  "As AI deployments multiply, CIOs are discovering that the hardest decisions are not technical — they are portfolio trade-off decisions about where to invest scarce governance attention and capital. The recurring failure mode is treating AI as a growth initiative while letting foundational data infrastructure and risk controls lag behind, which compounds costs rather than containing them. For enterprise leaders, the actionable insight is to treat AI cost management as a first-class discipline equal to AI capability development — because budget overruns on AI projects are already a common pattern across industries. The key caveat: organizations that defer foundational investments to chase AI use cases are building on an unstable base that will require expensive remediation within 18-24 months.",
