        "execSummary":  "The most important finding here is not that AI is failing — it is that enterprises are scaling investment faster than they are scaling governance, measurement, and the organizational discipline to kill bad projects. Gartner\u0027s data shows a structural gap between AI ambition and AI execution that is widening, not closing, as budgets grow. For customer-support and operations leaders, this is a forcing function: if you cannot articulate a clear ROI metric for each AI initiative before you fund it, you are statistically likely to be in the 75% that cannot scale successfully. The caveat is that \u0027scaling successfully\u0027 is itself a poorly defined benchmark — organizations should define their own success criteria rather than benchmarking against industry averages that mask wide variation in use-case complexity.",
