        "execSummary":  "The 80% unreadiness rate for agentic AI is the headline, but the more important finding is why: it is not a technology problem — it is a process documentation, data hygiene, and change management problem. Organizations that have not yet mapped and cleaned up their core workflows cannot delegate them to autonomous agents, which means AI agent readiness is fundamentally an operational excellence problem disguised as an AI problem. For customer-support leaders who are actively piloting or planning AI agents, this data validates investing in process documentation and data normalization before agent deployment — not after. The risk for those who skip this step is deploying agents that automate broken processes at scale, amplifying rather than eliminating operational debt.",
